Both dbt and Spark produced the same number of orders (2,829) and the same total quantity (8,615). However, their schemas are slightly different.

UUID: dbt uses the UUID type, while Spark stores these identifiers as STRING because it does not support a native UUID type.

Timestamp: dbt uses TIMESTAMP WITH TIME ZONE, while Spark uses TIMESTAMP.

Other columns: quantity and product have the same data types in both systems.

These differences can affect data compatibility. Users may need to convert data types or rename columns when working with both outputs.
